meta {
  name: Source Resolve
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/apis/{{site}}/api/copilot/source
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "token": "guideline:protocol-htn-v1#htn.bp-target",
    "patient_uuid": "{{patientUuid}}"
  }
}

docs {
  # Source Resolve

  UC6/UC7 — `POST /api/copilot/source`, the click-to-source resolver.
  Requires the `user/source.write` scope (deliberately "write", not
  "read" — the core dispatcher derives a POST's required action as
  `create`; see Bootstrap::registerApiScopes()) and the `patients`/`med`
  ACL. Resolves the SAME token minted by `ReferenceIndex::tokenFor()` and
  shipped in every Turn response's `refs[].token` into the smallest
  preview a clinician needs to verify a claim — re-grounded against LIVE
  data on every call, never a cached turn.

  ## This request's body: a guideline token (UC7)

  `guideline:protocol-htn-v1#htn.bp-target` resolves through the real,
  committed corpus index to the chunk's heading + a bounded snippet of
  its body — never the whole chunk (minimum-necessary evidence applies to
  previews too).

  ## Other token shapes to try (swap the body above)

  - Lab-PDF extraction citation (UC6), from a Document Upload response's
    `document_id`:
    ```json
    {
      "token": "lab_pdf:742#analytes[0].value",
      "patient_uuid": "{{patientUuid}}"
    }
    ```
    Resolves to `{type: "document", document_id, filename, page, quote,
    field}` — refused with a generic "unknown source document" message
    (never a distinguishable error) if the document does not belong to
    `patient_uuid`, so there's no cross-patient enumeration side channel.

  - Intake-form extraction citation: same shape, `"token":
    "intake_form:<document_id>#<field_path>"`.

  - Deterministic finding citation: `"token":
    "detector:panic-potassium-high"` — resolves to a typed, PHI-minimal
    `{type: "detector", finding_id, label}` with NO database read at all.

  - Plain chart pointer: `"token": "procedure_result:lab-potassium"` —
    resolves to `{type: "chart", source_type, source_id}`, no value
    fetched.

  A malformed token (missing `:`), a required-but-missing `#field`
  fragment, or an unresolvable id all fail loud with a generic 400 — never
  a guessed preview.
}
